---
// The publication's identity page: what this is, what it is not, and where the figures come
// from. Exists for readers first, and second for the search and answer engines that need an
// entity to attach the work to. Plain register, no em-dashes, no self-congratulation.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ORG, DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION } from "../lib/seo.mjs";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About, Owner Scorecard"
  description={DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION}
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    name: "About Owner Scorecard",
    mainEntity: ORG,
  }}
>
  <section class="about">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      Owner Scorecard is an independent research publication. It lays a business out the way an
      owner would read it: roughly a decade of revenue, margins, returns on capital, owner
      earnings, buybacks, share count, and debt, every figure traced to the company's own SEC
      filings.
    </p>

    <p>
      What you will not find here is a rating, a price target, an estimate, or a buy or sell.
      That is not an oversight. The old Value Line sheet earned its place on Warren Buffett's
      desk for its record table, not for the ranks and timeliness scores printed beside it. This
      publication keeps the record and leaves out the rest. The facts are presented; the judgment
      is the reader's.
    </p>

    <p>
      The figures come from primary sources: annual and quarterly reports filed with the SEC, and
      the equivalent filings for the Japan and ADR catalogs. Where a number is computed, the
      <a href="/concepts">Principles</a> page defines the computation. Where a company's own
      disclosure is thin, the page says so rather than papering over it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Research Notes are published under the publication's name. Errors, once found, are
      corrected in place, the note's updated date is changed to say so, and the change is logged
      in the public <a href="/corrections">corrections record</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="fine">
      Owner Scorecard is not registered as an investment adviser or broker-dealer. Nothing here
      is investment advice or a recommendation to buy or sell any security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .about { max-width: 640px; }
    .about h1 { margin: 0 0 16px; }
    .about p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .fine { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
